    What it does (per SPEC):
    - recommend_next_product(report) -> NextProduct — deterministic. Picks dominant product (max revenue from report.top_products), detects its category via SPEC keyword priority (template > pdf > pack/bundle > course/tutorial > other), then scans report.questions in order. First question carrying a category keyword wins -> builds that format (e.g. "Wedding Planners Template"), citing the real question verbatim in evidence. No match -> category extension of the winner ("Notion Template Pack 2"). Graceful at every empty boundary: empty questions, empty top_products, both empty ("New Digital Product").
    - build_recommender_prompt(report) -> str — strict-JSON instructions + full report embedded via json.dumps(report.model_dump()).
    - Imports only core.models + stdlib (json, re).
    
